{"ld": 429, "paper": "HP283", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Track Certain Information Regarding and Seek Federal Reimbursement for Medical Care Provided to Asylum Seekers", "sponsor_id": "h-drinkwater-gary", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bernard-susan", "h-boyer-david", "h-foley-robert", "h-haggan-kimberly", "h-hall-randall", "h-mason-richard", "h-poirier-jennifer", "h-quint-tracy", "h-thorne-james"], "committee_code": "HHS", "committee_name": "Health and Human Services", "summary": {"text": "This bill requires a hospital to collect information from a patient seeking care regarding the patient's immigration status. The hospital must inform the patient that the patient is not required to provide this information and that declining to provide this information does not preclude a patient from receiving medical care. The hospital must also inform the patient that the patient's immigration status does not affect the patient's ability to receive medical care at the hospital. A hospital must, by January 1, 2027 and on a quarterly basis thereafter, provide a report to the Department of Health and Human Services providing the aggregate cost of medical care provided to patients who are asylum seekers. The department is required to provide, by March 1, 2027 and annually thereafter, a report to the Governor and to the joint standing committee of the Legislature having jurisdiction over health and human services matters that provides information on the aggregate cost of medical care provided to patients who are asylum seekers. The department is required to establish routine technical rules to implement the requirements of this legislation.\n\nThe bill also requires the department, by July 1, 2027 and annually thereafter, to submit a written request to the United States Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services seeking reimbursement for the aggregate cost of medical care provided to asylum seekers during the prior year.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0283&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "final_disposition": {"label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "date": "2025-05-20", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 429)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0283&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}], "amendments": [], "committee_actions": [{"date": "2025-04-15", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": null}, {"date": "2025-04-15", "action": "Voted", "result": "Divided Report"}, {"date": "2025-05-12", "action": "Reported Out", "result": "ONTP/OTP"}], "committee_reports": [{"label": "Majority report", "recommendation": "Ought Not To Pass", "signer_count": 8, "signers": ["Senator Henry Ingwersen (Chair)", "Representative Michele Meyer (Chair)", "Representative Flavia DeBrito", "Representative Anne Graham", "Representative Julie McCabe", "Senator Tim Nangle", "Representative Daniel Shagoury", "Representative Sam Zager"], "signer_ids": ["s-ingwersen-henry", "h-meyer-michele", "h-debrito-flavia", "h-graham-anne", "h-mccabe-julia", "s-nangle-timothy", "h-shagoury-daniel", "h-zager-samuel"]}, {"label": "Minority report", "recommendation": "Ought To Pass", "signer_count": 5, "signers": ["Representative Lucien Daigle", "Representative Abigail Griffin", "Representative Kathy Javner", "Representative Michael Lemelin", "Senator Marianne Moore"], "signer_ids": ["h-daigle-lucien", "h-griffin-abigail", "h-javner-kathy", "h-lemelin-michael", "s-moore-marianne"]}], "chamber_actions": [{"date": "2025-02-04", "chamber": "House", "action": "Committee on Health and Human Services suggested and ordered printed."}, {"date": "2025-02-04", "chamber": "House", "action": "The Bill was REFERRED to the Committee on HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES."}, {"date": "2025-02-04", "chamber": "House", "action